Patch 2011: optional write-back of small main-memory colour render targets to guest memory (RT_READBACK=1, default OFF).

The game's exposure loop (PPU) reads the average-luminance target that the post chain draws into main memory. The backend never
wrote any render target back, so the PPU averaged zeros. This copies such a target to guest memory after the frame.

